--TEST--
A write to the variable at the start of a narrowed `readonly` path makes the property nullable again, and `->` on it is an error — `rule:types/narrowing`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// After `$holder` gets a new object, the test no longer says anything about
// `$holder->node`, so the second `->` does not compile.
final class Node
{
    public function label(): string
    {
        return "node";
    }
}

final class Holder
{
    public function constructor(public readonly ?Node $node) {}
}

final class Probe
{
    public static function show(Holder $holder): string
    {
        if ($holder->node != null) {
            echo $holder->node->label(), "\n";
            $holder = new Holder(null);
            return $holder->node->label();
        }
        return "empty";
    }
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0459]: `null|Node` may be `null`, so `->` cannot reach a member of it
   --> case.nvs:24:20
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
